   "hypothesis_id": "BTBD9_ACO1_iron_homeostasis",
   "mechanism": "Restless legs syndrome is fundamentally linked to brain iron deficiency. BTBD9, a major genetic risk factor for the disease, interacts physically with ACO1, a bifunctional cytosolic iron sensor. Disruptions in BTBD9 alter ACO1-mediated regulation of iron-responsive elements, perturbing neuronal iron uptake and utilization. This localized iron deficiency drives the abnormal nervous system electrophysiology and sleep behaviors characteristic of RLS.",
